/srv/square is a directory every member can write to. Notes, scripts,
a story written by three people, whatever you like:

  echo "hello from $USER" > /srv/square/hello-$USER.txt

Only you can delete or rename what's yours there. For a project with
other people, make a directory everyone in it can add to:

  mkdir /srv/square/zine && chmod g+w,+t /srv/square/zine

Files in it get the members group, so g+w lets others add theirs, and
+t keeps anyone from deleting someone else's. It all counts toward your
quota and isn't backed up. Read /srv/square/README.
